  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "cmhe9CquU7e1O8m5JFyh3owUS5E=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:43.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The reactor's internal `IEventBus` uses numeric event ids grouped into ranges. `ReactorEventTypes` occupies the 10000 range and `SyncEventTypes` the 20000 range:\n\n| Enum | Members |\n| --- | --- |\n| `QueueEventTypes` | `JOB_AVAILABLE` 10000 |\n| `ReactorEventTypes` | `JOB_PENDING` 10001, `JOB_RUNNING` 10002, `JOB_WRITE_READY` 10003, `JOB_READ_READY` 10004, `JOB_FAILED` 10005, `READMODEL_BATCH_COMPLETED` 10006, `READMODEL_INDEXED` 10007, `MODEL_LOADED` 10008 |\n| `SyncEventTypes` | `SYNC_PENDING` 20001, `SYNC_SUCCEEDED` 20002, `SYNC_FAILED` 20003, `DEAD_LETTER_ADDED` 20004, `CONNECTION_STATE_CHANGED` 20005 |\n| `JobExecutorEventTypes` | `JOB_STARTED` 20000, `JOB_COMPLETED` 20001, `JOB_FAILED` 20002, `EXECUTOR_STARTED` 20003, `EXECUTOR_STOPPED` 20004 |\n\nThe trap is the last row. **Two distinct `JobFailedEvent` shapes exist**, and they differ in the type of the `error` field:\n\n- `ReactorEventTypes.JOB_FAILED` (10005) carries `error: Error`.\n- `JobExecutorEventTypes.JOB_FAILED` (20002) carries `error: string`.\n\nSo `event.error.message` is correct for one and silently `undefined` for the other. Check which enum you subscribed to before reading `error`. Most application code should subscribe to `ReactorEventTypes`; `JobExecutorEventTypes` is the lower-level executor-lifecycle set, emitted by the executor managers for individual job execution and executor startup/shutdown.\n\nWorth flagging: the \"10000 vs 20000 range\" framing is a useful mnemonic but not a guarantee of uniqueness. `JobExecutorEventTypes` also lives in the 20000 range and its numbers **collide** with `SyncEventTypes` \u2014 `JOB_COMPLETED` and `SYNC_SUCCEEDED` are both 20001, `JOB_FAILED` and `SYNC_SUCCEEDED`/`SYNC_FAILED` overlap at 20002/20003. Treat the enum you import, not the number, as the identity.\n\nSubscribers are called sequentially in registration order. `emit()` collects thrown subscriber errors and rejects once with an `EventBusAggregateError` whose `.errors` array holds them.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/01-WorkingWithTheReactor.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/04-Reference/01-Reactor/03-AdvancedReactorUsage.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:43.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:43.000Z"
    }
  },
